  "correction_to_the_record": "The factory's decision log (D-CANON-READ3) said a stopped stock is scored at zero for its last month, flattering a book that buys what has fallen, and that the confirmation would address this in its vote. Measured before any half-B alignment, the first statement is wrong in its mechanism and the second is withdrawn. The builder calls a stock stopped precisely when it has NO observation in the next month, so there is no later trade to recover; a stock's fall to its last trade is already inside its ordinary monthly return; and a stopped row earns exactly zero under the registered scoring, so no part of a gross result can come from stopped names. 163 stopped rows fall in the 96 scored months, 0.17 per cent of 96,000, and of those 161 carry an acquisition or merger action within 45 days of the last price date while exactly 1 carries a for-cause type: the cohort is taken over, not wound up, so a flat loss would have had the wrong sign. A key that moves the vote by a few basis points on an assumed loss is not a test. The exposure is reported by S1 to S3 and never voted.",
